en:{label:"SEO ARTICLE · PRACTICAL GUIDE",title:"How to use HipoBuy carefully: from product link to international parcel",lead:"A fact-led guide to the public workflow before you pay.",heads:["1. Start with a link that can be checked","2. Review the warehouse stage promptly","3. Treat the return window as a deadline","4. Consolidate only after each item is checked","5. Price and delivery time are not fixed promises","6. Use a staged buyer checklist"],paras:["HipoBuy’s public flow starts with a product link, product name or order reference. Record the exact colour, size, quantity and seller note before payment, then compare them with the live listing. Stock, seller price and domestic delivery can change before an order is completed.","HipoBuy says goods from different merchants can arrive at its warehouse, where acceptance and quality-inspection information is provided. Check the received item, count, visible colour, size label, packaging and obvious condition while the item is still stored. Inspection evidence is useful, but it cannot guarantee fit, authenticity or long-term performance.","Its public returns guide describes a five-day window for eligible warehoused items, counted from the next hour after the status changes and described as 120 hours. Eligibility depends on the seller’s return guarantee, item condition and the actual order. Do not assume that customised goods, removed packaging, or personal items such as socks are eligible.","Stored items can be combined into individual parcels. Make that choice after reviewing each warehouse record, rather than using consolidation as a shortcut. List the items, variants, visible issues and destination before selecting a route; dimensions and category restrictions may change the sensible parcel plan.","International charges and available routes depend on the destination and the finished parcel. Use the live Shipping Estimate or Charges page with current data, and leave room for dimensional weight, carrier changes, taxes and customs processing. Do not promise a universal freight cost, arrival date or customs outcome.","Keep the product link, selected variant and order notes. Review warehouse evidence early; raise an issue before submission where possible. Before international shipping, confirm parcel contents, consult the current estimate and read destination rules. The live order and policy pages control the final terms."],faqLabel:"FACT-LED FAQ",faqTitle:"HipoBuy: practical questions before you submit a parcel",faqLead:"Answers based on public guidance; live order terms control.",qs:["What does HipoBuy do after I submit a product link?","Can I combine goods from several sellers?","Do warehouse photos guarantee quality?","How long is the eligible return window?","Is every warehoused item returnable?","What can a buyer-requested return cost?","How is international shipping priced?","Can a delivery date be guaranteed?","Who handles customs and taxes?","What is the best first-time-buyer habit?"],as:["It describes a process of third-party purchase assistance, warehouse arrival, acceptance and inspection, then parcel selection and international shipping.","Its public description says items from different merchants can be stored and later combined into individual parcels.","No. They can show visible details, but not guarantee fit, materials, authenticity or long-term performance.","The public guide describes five days after the order becomes Warehoused, beginning the next hour; it calls this 120 hours for eligible cases.","No. Seller guarantee, product condition, warehouse time and category restrictions all matter.","The public guide lists return shipping to the seller, the seller’s original shipping cost and a 5 RMB service fee for an unconditional return; check the live request.","Use the current Shipping Estimate or Charges page with the real destination and parcel details.","No. Route availability, packed dimensions, carriers and customs can change the result.","Destination rules vary. Check current route information and your own local requirements.","Record the exact variant, review warehouse evidence promptly, and submit a parcel only after checking every item."]},
